{"name":"Rose Coloured Glasses","hex":"#e5c4c0","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"},{"term":"coloured","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["British standard spelling of colored."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of colored."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coloured"},{"term":"glasses","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of glass"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Spectacles, frames bearing two lenses worn in front of the eyes.","Field glasses; binoculars."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glasses"}],"entries":[{"title":"Optimism","blocks":[{"text":"Optimism is the attitude or mindset of expecting events to lead to particularly positive, favorable, desirable, and hopeful outcomes. A common idiom used to illustrate optimism versus pessimism is a glass filled with water to the halfway point: an optimist is said to see the glass as half full, while a pessimist sees the glass as half empty. In ordinary English, optimism may be synonymous with idealism—often, unrealistic or foolish optimism in particular."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG/330px-Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optimism"},{"title":"Rosy retrospection","blocks":[{"text":"Rosy retrospection is a proposed psychological phenomenon of recalling the past more positively than it was actually experienced. The highly unreliable nature of human memory is well documented and accepted amongst psychologists. Some research suggests a 'blue retrospective' which also exaggerates negative emotions, creating a bipolar distortion of affective memory that depends on personality, time, and developmental stage."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosy_retrospection"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG/500px-Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG/1280px-Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG/500px-Glass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Half a glass of water, illustration of two different mental attitudes, optimism (half full) and pessimism (half empty)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlass_Half_Full_bw_1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/%D0%9E%D0%BF%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82_%D0%B8_%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%81%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82.jpg/500px-%D0%9E%D0%BF%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%82